Feature: Project Details Source Code Access
	Testing the Source Code Access feature for the Project Details portlet.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen PJD Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENPJDA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen DUP Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENDUPA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENPJDA"
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENPJDA"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen PJD Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen DUP Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENPJDA |
	| ZENDUPA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen PJD Automotive |
	| Zen DUP Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I automatically have all non Source Code Access users removed from the GitHub repository 
	* I log into gmail using the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	* I tear down all gmail messages with the title "is-support-integration invited you to is-support-integration/liferay-dxp"

Scenario: View source code access user
	New source code access users on an approved project should be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository.

	Given I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENPJDA" 
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I log into gmail using the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I go to gmail html mode
	And I go to the email message from the user "is-support-integration" containing the text "is-support-integration invited you to is-support-integration/liferay-dxp"
	And I accept the GitHub repository invitation using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	Then I should be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

Scenario: View source code access user added to closed project
	New source code access users on a closed project should be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository after project approval.

	Given I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values on a closed project
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I log into gmail using the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I go to gmail html mode
	Then I should not be able to see an email message containing the text "is-support-integration invited you to is-support-integration/liferay-dxp"
	And I should not be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

Scenario: View source code access user added to expired project
	New source code access users on an expired project should not be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository.

	Given I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENPJDA" 
	And I edit a project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive" and code "ZENPJDA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Digital Enterprise Production" 
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status 
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values on a closed project
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I log into gmail using the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I go to gmail html mode
	Then I should not be able to see an email message containing the text "is-support-integration invited you to is-support-integration/liferay-dxp"
	And I should not be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

Scenario: Delete source code access user
	Source code access users on an approved project and deleted should not be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository.

	Given I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENPJDA" 
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I log into gmail using the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I go to gmail html mode
	And I go to the email message from the user "is-support-integration" containing the text "is-support-integration invited you to is-support-integration/liferay-dxp"
	And I accept the GitHub repository invitation using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I delete the Source Code Access user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com"
	And I automatically have all non Source Code Access users removed from the GitHub repository 
	Then I should not be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

